- content_for :title, "Read in a batch · Money Bin"
/ The confirmation before "Read in a batch" (OcrBatchesController#new): how many receipts and batches, the
/ estimated cost, the wait, and what the provider keeps. Sending is a POST with the same filter.
= render "ui/page_header", title: "Read in a batch",
  description: "Send the unread receipts of this filter to be read together, at about half the price of reading them one at a time."

= render "ocr_batches/mode", capability: @capability

- if !@capability.available
  p.mt-6 = link_to "Back to the receipts", receipts_path(@filter.to_params)
- elsif @count.zero?
  .mt-6
    = render "ui/callout" do
      p.text-sm
        | No receipt in this filter is waiting to be read.
        =< link_to "Back to the receipts", receipts_path(@filter.to_params)
- else
  dl.data-table.mt-6
    .data-row
      dt Receipts
      dd = "#{pluralize(@count, 'receipt')} (#{pluralize(@images, 'photo')}): the unread ones of this filter, and the failed ones with no items to lose"
    .data-row
      dt Batches
      dd = "#{pluralize(@batches_needed, 'batch')} of at most #{@capability.max_receipts.clamp(1, 100)} receipts, sent one after the other (more if the photos are large)"
    .data-row
      dt Estimated cost
      dd
        - if @estimate
          = ocr_batch_estimate(@estimate.cost_usd)
          span.text-ink-muted =< "(at most #{ocr_batch_usd(@estimate.cost_usd_max.round(2, BigDecimal::ROUND_UP))} if every answer were as long as allowed). #{@estimate.basis}"
        - else
          span.text-ink-muted = "Not available: #{@estimate_error}"
    .data-row
      dt How long
      dd Usually minutes; up to a day. The receipts stay as they are until their results arrive, then update by themselves.
    .data-row
      dt What the provider keeps
      dd
        | The photos and the prompt go to #{@capability.providers.to_sentence} through OpenRouter, which keep them and the
        |  answers until the batch is deleted (at most #{@capability.retention_days} days). The app deletes each batch as
        |  soon as its results are stored. Nothing else is sent: no file names, no ids, nothing from the ledger.
  = render "ui/callout", class: "mt-6" do
    p.text-sm
      | While a receipt waits in a batch it is not read one at a time, and opening it does not queue OCR. You can still
      |  enter it by hand; the batch's result for it is then not used.
  .mt-6.flex.items-center.gap-3
    = ui_button_to ocr_batches_path(@filter.to_params), variant: :primary do
      = ui_icon "layers"
      span = "Send #{pluralize(@count, 'receipt')}"
    = ui_link_button "Cancel", receipts_path(@filter.to_params), variant: :ghost
